# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy this file to .env. Values already exported by the shell take precedence.
# To use a file elsewhere, set BVFX_ENV_FILE=/absolute/path/to/file.
# Never commit .env or paste secret values into logs, issues, or config objects.

# Auth for the Claude Agent SDK. Set ONE of these TWO names, and check it with:
#
#     python -m pipeline.preflight
#
#   CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN   subscription billing (Pro/Max). `claude setup-token`.
#                             Value starts sk-ant-oat01-
#   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY         pay-per-token API billing. console.anthropic.com.
#                             Value starts sk-ant-api03-
#
# THESE TWO NAMES ARE THE ONLY ONES READ. If both are set, the API KEY WINS (measured
# with a live call: both present → model claude-opus-5, billed to API credits).
#
# CLAUDE_API_KEY IS NOT A THING. Neither is ANTHROPIC_KEY, CLAUDE_TOKEN or
# CLAUDE_CODE_API_KEY. A key was once added here as CLAUDE_API_KEY and silently
# ignored; the stale OAuth token above was used instead, and that subscription was
# over its monthly spend limit. It did not error. The session reported
# subtype=success, cost=$0.0000, one turn, and the limit message came back as ordinary
# assistant text — so a build layer "succeeded" having built nothing and would then
# have paid the critic to score an empty scene. `pipeline.preflight` catches the dead
# variable name; `preflight.empty_success` catches the zero-cost/zero-tool result.
#
# Prefer the API key if you care about the cost numbers. MAX_BUDGET_USD (25.0, in
# build_agent.py) stops a layer that overspends, and it reads total_cost_usd off the
# SDK result — which is real money under an API key and not comparable to it under a
# subscription. `evals compare` weighs cost deltas the same way.
#
# A WRONG (not misnamed) key is expensive in wall time, not money: the CLI retries a
# 401 ten times with backoff, ~190s, before it gives up — per call. If a run seems to
# hang before anything renders, check the key first.
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Asset generation (optional — the pipeline degrades to procedural geometry without these)

# image→3D (Meshy). Without it the asset stage can't build hero meshes.
MESHY_API_KEY=

# Image generation for isolation/concept art: codex (default) or higgsfield.
# `codex` needs no key — it borrows the Codex CLI's own ChatGPT login, so run
# `codex login` ONCE and it stays working: tokens refresh (and the rotation is
# persisted) automatically. `higgsfield` likewise uses the higgsfield CLI's auth.
# Check anytime with: python -m pipeline.assets.codex_auth
ASSET_IMAGE_BACKEND=codex

# Runtime configuration (optional)
# BLENDER_BIN=blender
# HIGGSFIELD_BIN=higgsfield
# BVFX_NO_TRANSCRIPT=0
# BVFX_DISTILL_INLINE=0
